7. Interview questions and answers
Q1. What are the three main types of Machine Learning?
Supervised learning learns from labeled data, unsupervised learning discovers patterns in unlabeled data, 
and reinforcement learning learns a strategy through actions and rewards.

Q2. What is the difference between classification and regression?
Classification predicts a category, such as fraud or legitimate. Regression predicts a numerical value, such as a house price.

Q3. What is K-Means?
K-Means is an unsupervised clustering algorithm that partitions data into a specified number of clusters based on distances to cluster centers.

Q4. Why is K-Means sensitive to feature scaling?
K-Means relies on distances. Features with larger numerical scales can dominate those distances, so scaling can help give features more comparable influence.

Q5. What is a reward in Reinforcement Learning?
A reward is numerical feedback from the environment that helps an agent learn a strategy for maximizing cumulative reward over time.
Q6. Can an AI project combine supervised and unsupervised learning?
Yes. For example, a bank could use clustering to explore customer segments and a supervised classifier to predict churn. The two methods address different tasks.

